WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:03.723
You've just been hired by an online
bookstore to build and maintain

2
00:00:03.723 --> 00:00:07.940
databases that can store information
on millions of books and customers.

3
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:11.803
But how do we even begin to create and
altar databases that store constantly

4
00:00:11.803 --> 00:00:16.740
expanding information or process millions
of orders from all over the world?

5
00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.965
The answer to these questions lies
in Sequel create and read commands.

6
00:00:20.965 --> 00:00:25.517
In this video, you'll learn how to create
a database using sequel syntax and

7
00:00:25.517 --> 00:00:29.440
you'll also discover how to drop or
delete database.

8
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.240
However, before you create a database, you
first need a clear idea of its purpose.

9
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:38.729
For example if you're building a database
for an online bookshop then your

10
00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:44.540
database needs to record data like book
titles, authors, customers and sales.

11
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.650
The data on these topics
must be stored and

12
00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:49.540
organized in relevant
tables in a database.

13
00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:53.840
Users can then access, retrieve and
update the data as needed.

14
00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:57.577
So how can you create
a database using Sequel Syntax?

15
00:00:57.577 --> 00:01:02.840
To create a database, just type
the Create and Database keywords.

16
00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.640
These keywords are then followed
by the name of your database.

17
00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.040
But what about removing or
dropping a database?

18
00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:14.940
To drop a database,
just type the keywords Drop and Database.

19
00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.940
Then follow these keywords with the name
of the database you want to remove.

20
00:01:18.940 --> 00:01:22.144
Let's look at these key words in action.

21
00:01:22.144 --> 00:01:25.354
To create a database,
I need to use Sequel Syntax.

22
00:01:25.354 --> 00:01:30.940
To demonstrate, let's create a second
book store database using Sequel Syntax.

23
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:33.071
First I type the keywords Create and

24
00:01:33.071 --> 00:01:36.740
Database followed by
the name of my new database.

25
00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:42.040
In this case the database
is called bookstore2_ db.

26
00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:46.440
I always use a meaningful and relevant
name when creating a new database.

27
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.640
This helps to make it
easier to document my work.

28
00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:55.040
Database names must also be unique and
can only have a maximum of 63 characters.

29
00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.673
If my database name doesn't
meet these requirements,

30
00:01:57.673 --> 00:02:00.040
then an error message will appear.

31
00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.740
Finally I add a semicolon to
the end of the statement.

32
00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.258
Then I run the statement.

33
00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:11.540
And the new database bookstore_db2,
appears on the left hand side bar.

34
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.540
So I've created a second database.

35
00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:17.940
I can also remove databases
using sequel statements.

36
00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:20.340
First I select the sequel tab.

37
00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:23.740
Then I input my query in
the code box that appears.

38
00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.343
I type the keywords Drop and

39
00:02:25.343 --> 00:02:29.041
Database followed by the name of
the database I want to delete.

40
00:02:29.041 --> 00:02:32.540
In this case it's bookstore_db.

41
00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:36.282
Now I run the query then
sequel deletes the database.

42
00:02:36.282 --> 00:02:41.740
In this video you learned how to create
and delete databases using Sequel Syntax.

43
00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.250
Great work.